      "writtenOn": "2020-04-10T16:15:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SDM845 uses PDC and you would need that to resume from wakeup capable GPIOs, if we ever suspend with deep idle states. The PDC driver patch was submitted here -\nhttps://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/11247151/\n\nThe TLMM interrupt controller should setup the mapping to PDC (as its parent), which was possibly merged later than 5.4 is here -\nhttps://lkml.org/lkml/2019/11/15/1085\n\nDo we see any problems exporting the symbol?",
      "parentUuid": "fa8da9d7_f080eb18",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 512,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 512,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "81535bd8a5b965cec2a957bdb5d5419d1160e2ca",
